S1's rank and return everyone who moved by more than 5 places."}, {"id": "S12", "text": "Using a CTE, build a 3-stage funnel per marketplace: orders placed -> orders kept (Delivered and not returned) -> customers who reordered within 90 days of that delivery."}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Rank the 20 listing managers by delivered GMV (sum of order_value on Delivered lines). Return name, category, marketplace, GMV and rank."}, {"id": "S4", "text": "Build a category x month table of contribution margin %. Flag every cell that is negative and say which category/month combinations are responsible for the loss."}, {"id": "S11", "text": "Customer lifetime value: total contribution per customer across all their orders, averaged by acquisition cohort (customers whose first order was a Diwali line at 35%+ off vs everyone else), plus the number of customers in each cohort."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Order Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D2", "text": "On the same screen show customer context: new vs repeat, city and state, acquisition channel, payment mode, review rating and comment, and any remarks."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a search box that takes an Order ID and shows the full story of that one line: product and listing manager, the price chain (MRP -> discount -> selling price -> ex-GST revenue), the cost stack (COGS, fee, shipping, packaging, ad spend, return costs) and the resulting contribution as a waterfall."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for Marketplace, Category, Campaign, Listing Manager and Order Status that combine with the date filters (AND logic) rather than replacing them."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a date-range filter on Order Date and a separate date-range filter on Delivery Date, and make sure both can be applied together."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Make the order-results table itself filterable and sortable by any visible column, so someone can browse instead of only searching by exact Order ID."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Analytics", "tasks": [{"id": "D9", "text": "Add a category x month heatmap of contribution margin %, with negative cells unmistakable at a glance."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "Add a geography panel: contribution and return rate by state, with the best and worst five cities called out."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "Add a monthly trend panel showing booked revenue and contribution together, so a viewer can see the month where they move in opposite directions."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Add a marketplace comparison panel: fee %, shipping, return rate and contribution per order for Amazon.in, Flipkart, Own Website and Meesho."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "Add a returns panel: return rate by reason, by payment mode and by month, plus the rupee leakage each one represents."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "Add a customer-cohort panel: first-order discount band vs 90-day repeat rate and average lifetime contribution."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a listing-manager leaderboard showing GMV, contribution and contribution margin % side by side, so 'best' is never reduced to one number the viewer can't question."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect a global date-range filter (Order Date), so the whole analytics page can be viewed for any period, not just the full year."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Add a channel and ads panel: ad spend, ROAS and contribution after ad spend per Acquisition Channel."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "Add a discount-depth panel: average contribution per line and return rate by discount band, with the line count shown so nobody over-reads a thin band."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format: Word, PDF, Notion, a README) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you went from the raw export to cleaned data to SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made, especially how you resolved listing-manager and customer identity; (2) **Key Discoveries**: your top 3-5 findings, stated the way a decision-maker wants to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations**: at least 3 concrete, data-backed recommendations for what Nivaas Home should do before next Diwali. This is the deliverable a hiring manager would actually read, so treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S1", "text": "Simulate a 30% discount cap on Air Fryers and Induction Cooktops during the Diwali peak. State your assumption about how much volume you would lose, then estimate the contribution you would have made instead."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Compare couriers and warehouses on delivery time and return rate. Does a slower courier cause more returns, or is the difference explained by marketplace and category mix?"}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Test the pull-forward theory: did November and December volume dip because Diwali buyers had already bought? Compare against the other non-sale months and be honest about what the data can and cannot prove."}]}], "premium": [{"id": "X2", "text": "**Prove the COD gap is real.** COD orders return, cancel and RTO far more often than prepaid ones. Run a statistical test (chi-square or two-proportion z-test) and decide whether the gap survives once you control for marketplace and category mix. Show your work."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Build and defend a manager scorecard.** Combine GMV, contribution margin, return rate and ad efficiency into one weighted score. Run a sensitivity analysis showing how the ranking changes as you vary each weight by +/-10%, and say which weighting you would recommend and why."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Quantify discount elasticity.** Does a deeper discount buy proportionally more volume, or does the company give away more margin than it wins back? Quantify the relationship by category, not just describe it."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Normalize it.** Design a 3NF relational schema (separate tables for listing managers, customers, SKUs and order lines at minimum) from the flat file, load it into a real SQL database, and rewrite your S3 and S10 answers as proper JOIN queries."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Forecast next quarter.** Using the 12 months of history, forecast Q1 FY26-27 (Apr-Jun 2026) booked revenue and contribution per marketplace, treating the Diwali spike sensibly rather than letting it distort the trend."}]}$pack$::jsonb
