: "S4", "text": "Build a category x month table of contribution margin %. Flag every cell that is negative and say which category/month combinations are responsible for the loss."}, {"id": "S10", "text": "Cohort query: classify each customer by the discount on their FIRST order, then compute the share who placed a second order within 90 days. Use a fixed 90-day window and exclude customers acquired after 31 Dec 2025 so the comparison is fair."}, {"id": "S11", "text": "Customer lifetime value: total contribution per customer across all their orders, averaged by acquisition cohort (customers whose first order was a Diwali line at 35%+ off vs everyone else), plus the number of customers in each cohort."}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Rank the 20 listing managers by delivered GMV (sum of order_value on Delivered lines). Return name, category, marketplace, GMV and rank."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Order Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for Marketplace, Category, Campaign, Listing Manager and Order Status that combine with the date filters (AND logic) rather than replacing them."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a search box that takes an Order ID and shows the full story of that one line: product and listing manager, the price chain (MRP -> discount -> selling price -> ex-GST revenue), the cost stack (COGS, fee, shipping, packaging, ad spend, return costs) and the resulting contribution as a waterfall."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same screen show customer context: new vs repeat, city and state, acquisition channel, payment mode, review rating and comment, and any remarks."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Make the order-results table itself filterable and sortable by any visible column, so someone can browse instead of only searching by exact Order ID."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a date-range filter on Order Date and a separate date-range filter on Delivery Date, and make sure both can be applied together."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Analytics", "tasks": [{"id": "D11", "text": "Add a channel and ads panel: ad spend, ROAS and contribution after ad spend per Acquisition Channel."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a listing-manager leaderboard showing GMV, contribution and contribution margin % side by side, so 'best' is never reduced to one number the viewer can't question."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Add a marketplace comparison panel: fee %, shipping, return rate and contribution per order for Amazon.in, Flipkart, Own Website and Meesho."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "Add a customer-cohort panel: first-order discount band vs 90-day repeat rate and average lifetime contribution."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "Add a monthly trend panel showing booked revenue and contribution together, so a viewer can see the month where they move in opposite directions."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "Add a returns panel: return rate by reason, by payment mode and by month, plus the rupee leakage each one represents."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect a global date-range filter (Order Date), so the whole analytics page can be viewed for any period, not just the full year."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "Add a discount-depth panel: average contribution per line and return rate by discount band, with the line count shown so nobody over-reads a thin band."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Add a category x month heatmap of contribution margin %, with negative cells unmistakable at a glance."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "Add a geography panel: contribution and return rate by state, with the best and worst five cities called out."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format: Word, PDF, Notion, a README) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you went from the raw export to cleaned data to SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made, especially how you resolved listing-manager and customer identity; (2) **Key Discoveries**: your top 3-5 findings, stated the way a decision-maker wants to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations**: at least 3 concrete, data-backed recommendations for what Nivaas Home should do before next Diwali. This is the deliverable a hiring manager would actually read, so treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S5", "text": "Identify SKUs that lose money at every discount level, and recommend which to drop, reprice or bundle."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Do review ratings predict returns? Find the SKUs whose reviews and return rates tell the same story, and the ones where they disagree."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Compare couriers and warehouses on delivery time and return rate. Does a slower courier cause more returns, or is the difference explained by marketplace and category mix?"}]}], "premium": [{"id": "X5", "text": "**Quantify discount elasticity.** Does a deeper discount buy proportionally more volume, or does the company give away more margin than it wins back? Quantify the relationship by category, not just describe it."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Normalize it.** Design a 3NF relational schema (separate tables for listing managers, customers, SKUs and order lines at minimum) from the flat file, load it into a real SQL database, and rewrite your S3 and S10 answers as proper JOIN queries."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Forecast next quarter.** Using the 12 months of history, forecast Q1 FY26-27 (Apr-Jun 2026) booked revenue and contribution per marketplace, treating the Diwali spike sensibly rather than letting it distort the trend."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Prove the COD gap is real.** COD orders return, cancel and RTO far more often than prepaid ones. Run a statistical test (chi-square or two-proportion z-test) and decide whether the gap survives once you control for marketplace and category mix. Show your work."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "